- Hemoglobin A1c (to detect occult diabetes despite patient denial — common in undiagnosed prediabetes/diabetes);  
- Serum albumin and prealbumin (to assess nutritional status — hypoalbuminemia impairs wound healing);  
- Complete blood count (to screen for anemia, chronic inflammation, or infection);  
- Basic metabolic panel (to evaluate renal function and electrolytes).  
Among these, A1c is especially high-yield: even without classic symptoms, hyperglycemia is a major contributor to non-healing ulcers and may be undiagnosed.

